       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose is unsafe as written. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up a lot, and there's no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours as needed**, for analgesia.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and any note to add, such as \"take with food.\" I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, please confirm it's intentional and give the clinical reason. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
